Trace Packet Lister: CS Decode library testing
-----------------------------------------------

** Library Version : 1.8.3

Test Command Line:-
/root/mahdi/DecodeWorkspace/OpenCSD/decoder/tests/bin/builddir/trc_pkt_lister   -help  

Trace Packet Lister - commands

Snapshot:

-ss_dir <dir>       Set the directory path to a trace snapshot
-ss_verbose         Verbose output when reading the snapshot

Decode:

-id <n>             Set an ID to list (may be used multiple times) - default if no id set is for all IDs to be printed
-src_name <name>    List packets from a given snapshot source name (defaults to first source found)
-multi_session      List packets from all sources - assumes same config for all (ignored if -src_name used)
-dstream_format     Input is DSTREAM framed.
-tpiu               Input from TPIU - sync by FSYNC.
-tpiu_hsync         Input from TPIU - sync by FSYNC and HSYNC.
-decode             Full decode of the packets from the trace snapshot (default is to list undecoded packets only)
-decode_only        Does not list the undecoded packets, just the trace decode.
-o_raw_packed       Output raw packed trace frames
-o_raw_unpacked     Output raw unpacked trace data per ID
-src_addr_n         ETE protocol: Split source address ranges on N atoms
-stats              Output packet processing statistics (if available).
-no_time_print      Do not output the elapsed time for tests.

Consistency checks

-aa64_opcode_chk    Check for correct AA64 opcodes (MSW != 0x0000)
-direct_br_cond     Check for incorrect N atom on direct unconditional branches
-strict_br_cond     Strict conditional checks - look for incorrect N atom on all unconditional branches.
-range_cont         Range continuity checks - check next range after N atom is continuous.
-halt_err           Halt on bad packet error (default attempts to resync).

Development:
Options used during develop and test of the library

-profile            Mute logging output while profiling library performance
-test_waits <N>     Force wait from packet printer for N packets - test the wait/flush mechanisms for the decoder
-macc_cache_disable Switch off caching on memory accessor
-macc_cache_p_size  Set size of caching pages
-macc_cache_p_num   Set number of caching pages

Output:
   Setting any of these options cancels the default output to file & stdout,
   using _only_ the options supplied.

-logstdout          Output to stdout -> console.
-logstderr          Output to stderr.
-logfile            Output to default file - trc_pkt_lister.ppl
-logfilename <name> Output to file <name> 
